Theorem PL-1: Pipeline-ordering rule signatures — PL-1 through PL-11 + PL-1a + PL-4a

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS pipeline is a 12-step strictly-ordered DAG per Annex E §AIMS + arc.md sec-Pipeline
    - Step ordering is load-bearing: stale summaries forbidden (PL-5);
      adding a pass requires matched constraint update (PL-6)
    - TRMC normalization (Step 3a + Step 4a) adds the PL-7 through PL-11
      five-rule cluster for context-region detection + structural verify
      + rewrite + rollback + ContextBehavior derivation
    - 13 active PL theorems including PL-1a + PL-4a sub-rules per the
      section inventory table (line 107)

  Soundness property:
    PL-1 (interprocedural-first):
      type : List FunctionId -> Pipeline
      Steps 1-2 (analyze_program + apply_ownership) SHALL run once across
      all functions before any per-function step (3-12).

    PL-1a (per-function SCC topological order):
      type : CallGraph -> List FunctionId
      Per-function pipeline (Steps 3-12) processes functions in SCC
      topological order; callees realized before callers (load-bearing
      for FipContract Certified IFF post-realization-zero-unmatched check).

    PL-2 (Step 4 before Step 5):
      type : Function -> Pipeline
      analyze_function (Step 4) SHALL precede realize_rc_reuse (Step 5);
      state map drives emission.

    PL-3 (Step 5 before Step 9):
      type : Function -> Pipeline
      realize_rc_reuse (Step 5 phase 1) SHALL precede merge_blocks (Step 9);
      position-keyed entry_states / exit_states / instr_states are
      invalidated by merge.

    PL-4 (Step 10 after Step 9):
      type : Function -> Pipeline
      realize_annotations (Step 10 phase 2) SHALL follow merge_blocks
      (Step 9); phase 2 uses ArcVarId-keyed AimsStateMap lookups surviving
      merge (var_state_at_block_entry).

    PL-4a (Step 8a unwind_cleanup before Step 9):
      type : Function -> Pipeline
      unwind_cleanup (Step 8a) SHALL precede merge_blocks (Step 9);
      unwind cleanup alters CFG (invoke / resume edges).

    PL-5 (no stale summaries):
      type : Pipeline -> Bool
      no pass SHALL rely on stale summaries; if a pipeline step modifies
      IR or updates an effect summary, all downstream consumers MUST
      see updated values (verifier-before-input = sequencing bug).

    PL-6 (adding-a-pass meta-rule):
      type : NewPass -> List Constraint
      adding a pass requires updating ordering + proving no constraint
      violation; matched commit pair touching both pipeline + tests.

    PL-7 (TRMC normalization detect candidate):
      type : Function -> Option ContextRegion
      Step 3a TRMC normalization detects tail-recursive fns returning
      constructor applications; ContextBehavior 4-field record carries
      preserves_context / consumes_hole / requires_unique_context /
      may_resume_nonlinearly per Annex E §AIMS PL-7 + Leijen & Lorenzen
      JFP 2025.

    PL-8 (TRMC candidate predicate):
      type : Function -> Bool
      candidate = self-recursive + recursive call in tail position of
      constructor argument + constructor in return path; context region
      = span from recursive call to wrapping constructor.

    PL-9 (TRMC rewrite idempotency):
      type : Function -> Function
      candidate normalized to accept ContextHole parameter
      (Shape = ContextHole); INTERNAL ABI change; external calling
      convention preserved via wrapper thunk; idempotent.

    PL-10 (TRMC structural verify + rollback):
      type : Function -> Result Function (List VerifyError)
      structural verify (after Step 3a + Step 4 on rewritten IR):
        (a) ContextHole threaded correctly through recursive calls
        (b) no new allocations on allocation-free paths
        (c) rewritten CFG well-formed
        (d) function arity + calling convention preserved
        (e) constructor args evaluated in same order
      on failure: rewrite rolled back to pre-TRMC IR; Steps 3-4 re-run
      on restored CFG per PL-5 (no stale summaries).

    PL-11 (ContextBehavior initialization + join):
      type : List ContextBehavior -> ContextBehavior
      initial most-optimistic: <preserves_context=true, consumes_hole=true,
        requires_unique_context=false, may_resume_nonlinearly=false>;
      join: preserves_context(AND), consumes_hole(AND),
        requires_unique_context(OR), may_resume_nonlinearly(OR).

    Closes opencode S01-R0-F3 PL-category-omission finding: sec-07 dispatch
    consumes these 13 signatures + sec-07 discharges per-rule theorems
